{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts@L104","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":104,"end":108}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":104,"end":108},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:43e1eb03dac6eb1509febe843a33b45fb55e5b2026ec4d3abb39df0b895ab52a","meta":{"text":"Extract the RHS of an assignment expression.\nPL/SQL stores only the RHS in `expr` (e.g. `'APPROVE'`) — no `=` present → return as-is.\nC# stores the full statement, optionally with a type prefix (`decimal amount = rec.Amount` or\n`decision = \"APPROVE\"`) → return everything after the first standalone assignment `=`.\nA \"standalone `=`\" is one that is NOT part of `==`, `>=`, `<=`, `!=`, or `=>`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts@L121","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":121,"end":121}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":121,"end":121},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:59478fb506e1fbd543a38f3470dd0b165df1378f1112a02bad569aabd80b54e8","meta":{"text":"Build the normalized action signature for one rule."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts@L141","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":141,"end":142}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":141,"end":142},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:cdd0a197d1d6a02ad8422c7276ef95a19b6c30d61733455608b723817f8f74e9","meta":{"text":"Build the sorted normalized condition signatures for one rule. Loop conditions collapse to\n`<loop>` — the row source is not comparable across languages, only the structural role is."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts@L157","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":157,"end":157}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":157,"end":157},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a0a14564a67f476131e538088275108ac85556b78f9a2b9b86cd074e5671eceb","meta":{"text":"Full signature for a rule: conditions + action."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts@L170","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":170,"end":173}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":170,"end":173},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:01f1c8810cf5bf0d6dc870b7a56a7fe86be5842d5fe13ba7793c0c523ec6385d","meta":{"text":"Index `root` into a fresh temp soul and return the soul (caller must clean up `cribDir`). The\nfixture root is treated as a read-only repo — indexRepo discovers files but never writes into it."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts@L183","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":183,"end":189}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parity/parity.ts","span":{"start":183,"end":189},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:6c578c5658937a201308eae561f8617b599316128a3502a574b2acc6d7402b31","meta":{"text":"Run the decision-table parity comparison between the PL/SQL `assess_application` and the C#\n`AssessApplication` procedures. Returns the matched / only-PL/SQL / only-C# rule sets + equality.\nGreedy multiset match: each rule is matched at most once (a rule signature that appears N times on\none side matches at most N times on the other). Equal iff both only-* sets are empty."}}
